Landor is looking for a Senior Client Manager - 12 Month FTC Corporate Clients to join our London studio. Could this be you?&nbsp; &nbsp;

  &nbsp;

We are Landor, part of WPP

World-leading brand experts,&nbsp;
underpinned by the most expansive strategic &amp; creative capabilities in our category.

We make brands more valuable and less vulnerable.

We build brands differently. We work with our clients to define and solve their business problems through the lens of brand. We strategically join the dots between our design, experience, governance and measurement capabilities, and always connect our brand work to business outcomes.&nbsp;

Landor companies also include amp (sonic branding), bdg (workplace &amp; architectural experts), Deep Local (creative technologists) and ManvsMachine (3D motion design).

&nbsp;

About WPP

&nbsp;

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

&nbsp;

  &nbsp;

What you’ll do &nbsp;

The Senior Client Manager builds trusted, long-term relationships with corporate clients, developing a deep understanding of their businesses, brands, organizational priorities and challenges. They connect client needs with the agency’s capabilities to deliver impactful work, strengthen partnerships and support sustainable account growth.

&nbsp;

Key responsibilities

• Manage a portfolio of corporate client accounts within a larger portfolio.

• Build relationships with key client stakeholders and understand their business objectives, organizational context and decision-making needs.

• Identify opportunities to address clients’ brand and business challenges, grow existing accounts and contribute to new business pursuits.

• Develop clear, compelling proposals and scopes of work that define project objectives, deliverables, timing and investment.

• Partner with teams across the agency to deliver high-quality work on time, on budget and within scope.

• Communicate recommendations clearly and confidently, and help clients and internal teams align on feedback, refinements and project direction.

• Lead client status meetings and provide clear, consistent reporting to stakeholders.

• Ensure all client-facing communications and materials are accurate, polished, relevant and aligned with the agency’s brand.

• Coordinate with agency leadership and resource management to ensure projects are appropriately staffed and aligned with scope and budget.

• Work with client leadership to address pricing, payment and scope changes.

• Partner with Finance on invoicing, collections, timesheets, budget management, forecasts and revenue reporting.

• &nbsp;Maintain organized records of client deliverables, credentials and case studies.

&nbsp;

  &nbsp;

What you’ll need &nbsp;

&nbsp;

• Experience in a similar role within a brand consultancy, advertising agency , business consultancy or similar

• Comfortable managing stakeholders at varying levels up to brand manager level

• Excellent project management and relationship building skills, but respectful of and comfortable with ambiguity and changing priorities

• Strategic thinker - confident when inputting into strategic creative work, through the lens of the client’s brief, enabling them to input and recommend clear next steps and actions

• Appetite for understanding the Landor offer, for new information, new business and new ideas

• Financially savvy - can articulate and understand financial goals for the business and for team members

• Capable of motivating and encouraging junior team members

